Flutter AirPlay Linux host

Project source is licensed under GPL-3.0-only, except files with their own
notices. UxPlay and lychee_player acknowledgements are preserved in the root THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and bundled license assets.

The bundle ships lychee_player (MIT) and the LGPL-2.1-or-later FFmpeg its
release pins, built without GPL or nonfree components; their notices are in
lychee_player-NOTICES.txt. No FDK-AAC dependency is used.

The native player compiles in libplist (LGPL-2.1-or-later,
https://github.com/libimobiledevice/libplist) from the source release pinned
in native/dependencies.lock.json; its license is in libplist-LGPL-2.1.txt.

Linux links distribution-provided libraries rather than vendoring their code:
- GTK 3 / GLib: LGPL-2.1-or-later, https://www.gtk.org/
- PulseAudio: LGPL-2.1-or-later client libraries, https://www.freedesktop.org/wiki/Software/PulseAudio/
- Avahi: LGPL-2.1-or-later, https://avahi.org/
- OpenSSL: Apache-2.0 for OpenSSL 3, https://www.openssl.org/source/license.html
  (other platforms compile in BoringSSL instead, so BoringSSL-LICENSE.txt does not apply here)

